{%- comment -%}
  A catalogue cell, not a floating card: hairline rules, square corners, no
  shadow and no lift on hover. The product photographs already carry four
  different supplier design systems, so the frame around them stays silent.
  Numerals are tabular and wrapped in <bdi> because a Latin price inside a
  Hebrew RTL cell reorders without it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if product != blank -%}
  <article class="en-cell{% unless product.available %} is-sold-out{% endunless %}">
    <a class="en-cell__media" href="{{ product.url }}" aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }}">
      {%- if product.featured_image != blank -%}
        {%- assign product_alt = product.featured_image.alt | default: product.title -%}
        {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 900 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '260,380,540,720,900', sizes: '(max-width: 749px) 78vw, (max-width: 1024px) 33vw, 25vw', alt: product_alt, class: 'en-cell__primary-image' }}
        {%- if product.images.size > 1 -%}
          {%- assign second_image = product.images[1] -%}
          <img
            class="en-cell__secondary-image"
            data-en-secondary-image
            src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAAD/ACwAAAAAAQABAAACADs="
            data-src="{{ second_image | image_url: width: 900 }}"
            data-srcset="{{ second_image | image_url: width: 380 }} 380w, {{ second_image | image_url: width: 540 }} 540w, {{ second_image | image_url: width: 720 }} 720w, {{ second_image | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w"
            sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 33vw, 25vw"
            width="{{ second_image.width }}"
            height="{{ second_image.height }}"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt="{{ second_image.alt | default: product.title | escape }}"
          >
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'en-cell__placeholder' }}
      {%- endif -%}
      <span class="en-cell__flags">
        {%- if product.compare_at_price_max > product.price -%}<b class="en-cell__flag--sale">מבצע</b>{%- endif -%}
        {%- unless product.available -%}<b class="en-cell__flag--out">אזל מהמלאי</b>{%- endunless -%}
      </span>
    </a>

    <div class="en-cell__body">
      {%- if category_label != blank -%}<p class="en-cell__category">{{ category_label }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      <h3><a href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title }}</a></h3>
      <div class="en-cell__price">
        {%- comment -%}
          A "from 219.90" on a product whose real ceiling is 529.90 is a number
          the buyer finds has moved after they click, which is the cheapest
          possible way to spend the trust this store's first principle is built
          on. Both ends are stated instead: the span is the honest figure, and
          it also tells a scanning eye that larger sets exist without any
          claim being made about them.

          The whole range sits inside ONE bdi. Two separate ones would let the
          bidi algorithm reorder the pair around the dash in an RTL line, which
          would print the ceiling first and read as a price rise.

          Products whose variants are all the same price fall to the plain
          branch and show a single figure - which is also how the known
          mispriced deck-light set will render, leaving that fault visible
          rather than papering over it with a fake span.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if product.price_varies -%}
          <bdi dir="ltr" class="en-cell__span">
            <strong>{{ product.price | money }}</strong><span class="en-cell__to">–{{ product.price_max | money }}</span>
          </bdi>
        {%- else -%}
          <strong><bdi dir="ltr">{{ product.price | money }}</bdi></strong>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if product.compare_at_price_max > product.price -%}<s><bdi dir="ltr">{{ product.compare_at_price_max | money }}</bdi></s>{%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      One purchase verb for every buyable cell. "הוסף לסל" would be a lie here —
      the link opens the product page, it does not add to cart — and splitting
      the label by variant count made the grid read as two different components.
      A sold-out product keeps the viewing label: a buy CTA on an unbuyable
      product is the kind of false promise the copy council ruled out.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <a class="en-cell__action" href="{{ product.url }}">
      <span>
        {%- if product.available -%}
          לרכישה
        {%- else -%}
          לצפייה במוצר
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
      <span class="en-cell__arrow" aria-hidden="true">←</span>
    </a>
  </article>
{%- endif -%}
